**CRISPR-Cas9**: a guide RNA (~20 nt) directs the Cas9 nuclease to a complementary DNA sequence adjacent to a **PAM** site; Cas9 makes a double-strand break. The cell's repair — error-prone NHEJ (knockout) or HDR with a template (precise edit) — does the rest. (Doudna/Charpentier, 2012; Nobel 2020.) It is programmable cut-and-paste for genomes — with off-target cuts as the central safety concern.

