**Base editors** (2016–): deaminase fused to nickase-Cas9 — chemically convert one base to another (C→T, A→G) without double-strand breaks. **Prime editing** (2019): nickase fused to reverse transcriptase writes longer edits from an RNA template. Both reduce reliance on double-strand breaks — the field's direction is *precision without breakage*.

