**Magnetic confinement** (tokamaks, stellarators): hold a 100M°C plasma with magnetic fields — ITER (France, international) is the giant; stellarators (Wendelstein 7-X) trade engineering complexity for steadier plasma. **Inertial confinement**: crush fuel pellets with lasers — NIF's approach. Both chase the same figure of merit: **Q**, fusion energy out over heating energy in.

