The National Ignition Facility achieved **scientific breakeven** (December 2022, repeated since): fusion output exceeded laser energy delivered to the target. What it did *not* prove: wall-plug breakeven (lasers are inefficient), repetition rate (NIF fires ~daily; power needs ~10/second), or economics. A physics milestone, not an energy milestone — the distinction matters.

