**Non-invasive** (EEG, fNIRS): scalp signals — safe, but centimeters of skull blur everything; good for coarse control. **Semi-invasive** (ECoG): electrodes on the brain surface — better signal, requires surgery. **Invasive** (Utah arrays, Neuralink-style threads): single-neuron resolution, highest bandwidth, highest risk. The trade is always **bandwidth vs. invasiveness**.

