An **AI agent** wraps a model in a loop: observe state → reason/plan → **act via tools** (APIs, code execution, browsers) → observe results → repeat. The model supplies the policy; the scaffolding supplies memory, tools, and persistence. Capabilities come from the *system*, not the weights alone — which is why evals must test systems, not just models.

