**SpaceX's Falcon 9** (first booster landing 2015) cut orbital launch costs roughly an order of magnitude — from ~$10,000/kg toward ~$1,000/kg-class economics. **Starship** (fully reusable, super-heavy) aims for another order of magnitude; as of 2026 it was flying test and early operational missions with full rapid reusability still in work. The lesson: *reusability*, not new physics, moved the curve.

